WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.670
Wyoming has always been a state

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.943 position:58%
that emphasizes rugged individualism.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.100 position:67%
We're pretty libertarian, always have been.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.030
The Golden Hills of Wyoming,

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.140
an ever spinning wheel of fortune.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.783 position:77%
The coordinates mad world, adventurous, pioneers,

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:20.473
the renegade horse.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.800 position:59%
However, throughout Wyoming's history,

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.730 position:58%
commodities, not rugged individualism

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.560
has powered its economy.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.730 position:80%
The commodity that we got established on was cattle

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.900 position:67%
and the commodity that came into our future

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.473 position:84%
fairly shortly thereafter was oil, and then came coal.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.100 position:91%
We're struggling right now to transition with that history

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.590 position:70%
because we rely heavily on coal, oil, and gas

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.145
for most of our state's revenue.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.740 position:58%
There has been a long-term discussion

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.130
about diversifying our economy.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:00.030 position:88%
We've recognized that depletable resources we banked on,

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.333 position:84%
coal and oil and gas are eventually gonna be depleted.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:08.640 position:83%
Today, Wyoming is looking to embrace a new commodity.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.770 position:91%
We need to find alternative industries and viable sectors.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:16.160 position:80%
Both blockchain and cryptocurrency represent values

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.493
that Wyoming can get online with.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.060 position:58%
As the world of blockchain and crypto

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.880
goes more and more mainstream,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.430
the race for the state to be crown

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.813
in the most crypto-friendly is on.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.810 position:64%
When you think of crypto-friendly cities,

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:31.620 position:59%
you have to start with Miami, Florida.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.820
The Miami mayor, Francis Suarez.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.280 position:91%
I want us to differentiate ourselves as the crypto capital

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.180 position:58%
of the United States or of the world.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.810
New York City mayor, Eric Adams.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.010 position:56%
New York city is gonna be the center

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:44.163
of the cryptocurrency industry.

00:01:45.008 --> 00:01:47.773 position:64%
But that race is led by the Cowboy State.

00:01:48.792 --> 00:01:50.280
It's about philosophy on this one.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.100 position:83%
And it's the philosophy of that rugged individualism,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.640 position:92%
the independence, and the ability to really get things done

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.000 position:66%
for yourself and control your own destiny.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.560
You get that from a blockchain,

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.260
and you don't get that without it.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.950
My name is Caitlin Long,

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:18.560 position:59%
I'm co-founder Avanti Financial Group,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.100
which is a bank chartered to serve

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.370 position:58%
the digital asset industry in Wyoming

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.373
that will be operating in 2022.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.350
Caitlin Long was born in Wyoming,

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.190 position:56%
but spent the majority of her career

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.570 position:61%
working for Morgan Stanley in New York.

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:36.683 position:91%
However, she's always kept one foot back home in Cheyenne.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.115 position:81%
Wyoming has a really interesting history of leading.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.450 position:70%
Wyoming gave women the right to vote 50 years

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.630 position:58%
before the rest of the United States.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:49.420 position:81%
When Wyoming invented the limited liability company,

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:52.560 position:56%
new form of business entity in 1977,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.320 position:88%
it took about a decade for the rest of the United States

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.670
to follow Wyoming.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.860 position:88%
Here Wyoming is leading yet again in digital asset laws,

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.257 position:66%
we already are seeing other states follow.

00:03:02.257 --> 00:03:04.230
I think it won't even take a decade

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.460 position:72%
for the critical laws of Wyoming to be enacted

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.623 position:64%
by the other states in the United States.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.560 position:61%
Because of champions like Caitlin Long,

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:16.940
Wyoming is leading the charge

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.600 position:78%
when it comes to integrating blockchain and crypto

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.693
to U.S. law.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:24.270
When I got into Bitcoin,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.020 position:88%
got some early coins, decided when it started running up

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.480
in the previous bull market in 2017

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.650
to donate some appreciated Bitcoin

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:34.140 position:61%
to the University of Wyoming Foundation

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:38.310 position:66%
to fund scholarships for female engineers.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.310
And I thought,

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:42.700 position:81%
well, I'll just quietly use some of my Bitcoin gains

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.750
to help solve that problem.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:45.910
And the University of Wyoming

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.150 position:58%
just sort of shrugged their shoulders

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:48.240
and probably said something

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.460 position:56%
along the lines of "what's bitcoin".

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.480 position:86%
The University of Wyoming could not accept her donation

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.590 position:61%
because the state's money transfer laws

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.623
restrict certain kinds of assets.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.047
I said at the time,

00:04:00.047 --> 00:04:01.127
"We've gotta fix this

00:04:01.127 --> 00:04:03.127 position:67%
"because this Bitcoin thing is gonna be big

00:04:03.127 --> 00:04:04.620
"and you don't wanna miss it."

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.690 position:69%
We though, well, what are we doing that for?

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:06.523
That's ridiculous.

00:04:06.523 --> 00:04:08.260
So in 2016, we started to look at

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.050 position:56%
this Money Transmitter Act revision.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:14.110 position:89%
What started as an attempt to give back to her home state

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:15.570
ended with her leading the charge

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:19.870 position:86%
on Wyoming's cryptocurrency and blockchain regulations.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.908
We really started to realize that

00:04:21.908 --> 00:04:24.690 position:77%
there was an open landscape for developing policy

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.060 position:58%
around blockchain and digital assets.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.180
We got together at that point

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:31.170 position:78%
and we kinda formed this little collaborative team

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:34.410
of enthusiasts and policymakers

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:37.130 position:86%
that started planning for what a future could look like

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.840
with digital assets.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.970 position:75%
There were 90 people involved at the legislature

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.520 position:58%
and about 30 people who endorsed this

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.350 position:77%
outside of the legislature in the very beginning.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.500
Since that time,

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.600 position:66%
we put together the blockchain task force,

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.550 position:92%
and now we formalized it into a permanent select committee.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.070 position:67%
After fixing the money transmitter statute,

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.760 position:77%
the task force took on a whole host of other laws

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.073
concerning blockchain and crypto.

00:05:03.615 --> 00:05:04.950
There've been 24 laws

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:06.958 position:72%
passed in four different legislative sessions,

00:05:06.958 --> 00:05:08.920
but I'd say the most important ones

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:12.680 position:67%
are that Wyoming clarified the legal status

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:14.340
of digital assets.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.110 position:59%
We realized there was an open question

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:17.820
about what is a digital asset,

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.340 position:89%
what is a cryptocurrency when it comes to property rights

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.570
and statutes?

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.690 position:56%
If a court is looking at this asset,

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.420
what are they gonna do with it?

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:27.928
We defined it as property.

00:05:27.928 --> 00:05:30.650 position:78%
And that's the basis upon which financial services

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:31.540
can be built

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.390 position:69%
and just basically making the law compatible

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:36.313 position:77%
with the way the technology was actually working,

00:05:36.313 --> 00:05:38.092
very foundational.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.450
The next steps,

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.670 position:83%
to fundamentally change the banking system in Wyoming

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.483
and possibly the country.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.230 position:72%
We have something called a dual banking system

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:50.230
in the United States

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.050 position:63%
where some banks are chartered federally

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:54.440 position:67%
and some banks are chartered by the states.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.610 position:64%
But if an organization dealt with crypto,

00:05:56.610 --> 00:06:00.230 position:83%
they were not allowed to use the U.S. banking system.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.600 position:64%
If you had crypto, if you had blockchain,

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.730 position:80%
if you had any word associated with it in your name

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:08.160 position:70%
or your business model or your business plan,

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.480
you wouldn't get banked.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:12.530 position:86%
And if you can't get banked, you can't have a business.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:15.410 position:84%
So we created a whole new type of state chartered bank

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:17.760 position:75%
called a Special Purpose Depository Institution,

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.130
the SPDI bank.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.900 position:91%
It operates the core payment systems for the U.S. dollars,

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.600
specifically ACH and Fedwire.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:25.433
And right now,

00:06:25.433 --> 00:06:28.000 position:83%
there are no crypto companies that have direct access

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:28.833
to that.

00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:30.000
It's kept separate.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.380
So banks can access that,

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:33.986 position:67%
but they can't provide services for crypto.

00:06:33.986 --> 00:06:38.020 position:70%
It's a way to plug the digital asset industry

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.430 position:75%
into the traditional financial services industry

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.130
in a safe and sound manner.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:42.963
Importantly,

00:06:42.963 --> 00:06:44.970 position:61%
this would also give those crypto banks

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.100 position:56%
if they were to get this SPDI access

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.170
to the feds payment system.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.320
And that's really important

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:53.790 position:92%
because that would really cut down on the cost and the time

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:56.340 position:80%
that it takes for these transactions to go through.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:01.340 position:80%
If you go back to thinking about when you were kids

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:04.130 position:88%
and you were exchanging baseball cards with your friend,

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:04.963
what did you do?

00:07:04.963 --> 00:07:06.369 position:59%
You both held onto both baseball cards

00:07:06.369 --> 00:07:08.340 position:58%
and you both let go at the same time.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.530 position:63%
And then you had simultaneous settlement

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.360
of that trade of the baseball card.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:15.700 position:59%
Nobody owed a baseball card to anybody

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:18.641 position:73%
because the transaction happens simultaneously.

00:07:18.641 --> 00:07:21.539
The adults screwed that up

00:07:21.539 --> 00:07:23.130
and we should learn from the kids

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.840
because the kids had it right.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.760 position:77%
There's no reason why you should ever have an IOU

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:29.800
for the baseball card.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.730 position:77%
There's no reason why you should ever have an IOU

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.660
for a dollar payment.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:34.670
We have the technology

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:38.100 position:89%
to be able to do simultaneous settlement of a U.S. dollar

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.100
against other types of assets,

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.630
namely digital assets and others,

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:45.300 position:67%
but we don't have the capability to do that

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:47.053
because of the regulatory regime.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:49.670
And when I signed it,

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:53.110 position:94%
I was very excited because no one else had really done that.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.660 position:61%
Everybody else was trying to figure out

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.830 position:59%
how to shoe-horn digital asset custody

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.330
into an existing trust structure

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:03.503 position:75%
or into some sort of existing banking structure.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.030
Regrettably,

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:07.600
we see at the national level,

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.560 position:73%
that there's a tremendous amount of resistance.

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:12.120 position:70%
Crypto markets aren't actually an alternative

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.090
to our banking system.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.830 position:66%
They're a mirror of the same broken system

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.560 position:78%
with even less accountability and no rules at all.

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.410 position:61%
If you're buying stock for speculation,

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:22.970 position:81%
you'd be protected by rules against things like pump

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:23.890
and dump,

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:27.913 position:80%
but not when you're buying Bitcoin for speculation.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:31.060 position:59%
There are four chartered Wyoming SPDIs

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:34.200 position:88%
and none of us have been approved by the federal reserve

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.120
yet.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.200 position:61%
One of cryptocurrency's biggest hurdles

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.720
really is that it is so new.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.380 position:66%
The fact that it is such a turbulent asset

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:45.550 position:77%
can kind of spook some of traditional Wall Street

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:47.510
and professional money managers.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.800 position:91%
I do think they are risky. They're not backed by anything.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.200
The reason they see resistance

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.470 position:73%
is because we're creating a banking institution

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:57.700 position:56%
that doesn't require FDIC insurance.

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:00.020 position:69%
The reason it doesn't require FDIC insurance

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:02.910 position:61%
is because it's not able to be at risk.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:05.400
It's a 100% reserve,

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.610 position:64%
a hundred percent depository institution.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:11.263 position:69%
that's incapable of lending out those funds.

00:09:11.263 --> 00:09:14.738 position:75%
I've been back to Washington two or three times,

00:09:14.738 --> 00:09:18.163 position:70%
I've been told that we're getting very close.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:23.786 position:83%
I think that governors and bank presidents understand

00:09:23.786 --> 00:09:26.770 position:67%
how important it is that the United States,

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:27.780
not just Wyoming,

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:32.110 position:77%
but the United States actually jump ahead on this

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:34.230 position:59%
because we are losing ground to China.

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:36.010
If we don't get in the game soon,

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.710
we are gonna be playing catch up.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:41.820 position:88%
Wyoming's Crypto Industry has some allies in Washington,

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:45.180 position:89%
it's most famous, may be one of the state's own senators.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.130
I encourage people to buy and hold.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:50.100 position:84%
I encourage them to save Bitcoin for their retirement,

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:51.204
for their future.

00:09:51.204 --> 00:09:52.962 position:66%
It's not the Wyoming way to sit around and

00:09:52.962 --> 00:09:54.420
wait for change.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:56.930 position:75%
We wanna be innovative and we're gonna push back

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:58.680
as hard as we can against the feds.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:03.180
It's not just cryptocurrencies.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.590
Wyoming has taken the first step

00:10:04.590 --> 00:10:07.230 position:70%
towards recognizing companies, organizations,

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:10.920 position:73%
and even cities run entirely on the blockchain.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:14.070 position:63%
July 1st, Wyoming became the first state

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.990
to formally legally recognize

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:20.070 position:75%
decentralized autonomous organizations, or DAOs,

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:21.130
in our statutes.

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:23.600
And we created the DAO LLC.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:27.040 position:84%
It's a fancy way of saying you can establish a company

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:31.290 position:77%
using blockchain and put it under an LLC moniker.

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:34.902 position:83%
Wyoming really has been a leader in business activity

00:10:34.902 --> 00:10:37.130
for decades.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:40.590 position:67%
LLCs were first established in Wyoming law.

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:43.460 position:66%
And this is just an extension of that LLC.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:45.360 position:72%
We're kind of going back to the original roots

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.950 position:59%
of how do you let people self-organize

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:51.460 position:80%
and give them the ability to do a couple of things?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.090
The idea of a DAO

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:55.754 position:77%
is the idea that we're going to have some portion

00:10:55.754 --> 00:10:58.094
of our company's responsibilities

00:10:58.094 --> 00:11:03.090 position:67%
delegated to algorithms, programming, code,

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:05.900 position:59%
where code is going to run the company

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.870
as opposed to your manager

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:11.130 position:75%
or members that show up every day to the office.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.063 position:59%
We're just gonna turn it over to code.

00:11:14.274 --> 00:11:16.040
One of the biggest DAOs out there

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.670
that people know the most about

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:20.970 position:69%
is a group that's known as Constitution DAO.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.710 position:56%
They crowdsourced a bunch of funding

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:26.270 position:77%
to try to buy the U.S. Constitution at Sotheby's.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:29.900 position:94%
They actually raised over 40 million in less than two weeks.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:32.010 position:77%
We would really love to display that constitution

00:11:32.010 --> 00:11:33.170
at the University of Wyoming.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.230 position:77%
And so, even the governor of Wyoming got involved

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:39.180 position:75%
to try to basically market to the 15,000 people,

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:42.380 position:78%
each of whom had a vote on where the constitution,

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:44.010
if the Constitution DAO had won,

